      "content": "Behavior regression for `column === \"done\"` with no result (e.g., a task the user manually completes before any bot run). Original code returned green (treating any \"done\" task as success by default; red only when `result.status` is explicitly set to a non-success value). New code falls through to `return \"\"`, dropping the green ring entirely. The function's own JSDoc says \"完成（绿）\" and the workflow canvas design doc says \"done 绿+✔ / 失败红（result.status）\" — i.e. green is the default for the \"done\" column and red is only the failure override. Restore that default.\n\nSuggested fix: after the `!== \"done\"` early-return, only flip to red when `result.status` is explicitly set to a non-success value, otherwise return green. Also replace `!=` (already flagged) with `!==`.",
